2. Alternative Path 1: U.S. Air Strikes + Soviet Military 
Acceleration
Logic: If either military establishment dominates decision-making, this escalatory 
path becomes plausible. The U.S. military sees a closing window; Soviet military 
wants to complete deployment.
3. Alternative Path 2: U.S. Diplomatic Freeze + Soviet Public 
Denial
Logic: If diplomatic actors prevail, both sides might initially pursue face-saving 
measures through international forums while buying time, though this risks 
allowing the crisis to solidify.
